.TH elf_get_value 3 "ELF Library Functions" "QuickJS" "ELF Library Functions"

.SH NAME
elf_get_value \- Retrieve a value from a data structure based on its type

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <lib/elf.h>
.B #include <lib/uint64.h>
.B uint64_t elf_get_value(void* elf, void* ptr, unsigned off32, unsigned size32, unsigned off64, unsigned size64);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The .B elf_get_value function retrieves a value from a data structure based on its type.

The function takes six parameters:
.I elf
A pointer to the ELF file structure (not used in this function).
.I ptr
A pointer to the data structure containing the value.
.I off32
The offset of the value in the data structure for 32-bit mode.
.I size32
The size of the value in bytes for 32-bit mode.
.I off64
The offset of the value in the data structure for 64-bit mode.
.I size64
The size of the value in bytes for 64-bit mode.

The function returns the value as a uint64_t. If the size is not supported, the function returns 0.

.SH EXAMPLE
The following example demonstrates how to use the .B elf_get_value function:

.I
.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/elf.h>
#include <lib/uint64.h>

int main() {
  // Assume elf is a valid pointer to an ELF file structure
  uint32_t value32 = 0x12345678;
  uint64_t value64 = 0x123456789ABCDEF0;
  uint64_t ret;

  // Example for 32-bit mode
  ret = elf_get_value(elf, &value32, 0, sizeof(value32), 0, 0);
  printf("32-bit value: 0x%llx\n", ret);

  // Example for 64-bit mode
  ret = elf_get_value(elf, &value64, 0, 0, 0, sizeof(value64));
  printf("64-bit value: 0x%llx\n", ret);

  return 0;
}
.!
